Z||000015||Shaun41178||10-16-2001||03:55 PM||||Drexter, I am pretty certain you can not use the roller lifters in a Fiero designed (173) block.  You need a newer block that was designed for a roller cam.<P>You have those roller lifters from Crane with the anit-rotation bars but in a block not designed for a roller cam the retainers or even the lifters themselves will hit the lower intake manifold of the fiero.  You need to use the block from a 3100 or a 3400 fwd engine to use a roller cam. <P>Also if you plan on using the fiero timing cover you need to get a cam button to keep the cam walking forward.  I am guessing you don't know what a cam button is and if you dont' then I think you are over your head on this project for the time being.  if you do know then that is good.  But I am guessing you dont' since you don't know what Joe Torma meant when he said "adjusting every weekend"<P>But to answer your question there are no aftermarket roller cams for a 173 block you would have to use a 3100 cam from GM.  meaning you would have to go to a GM dealership to get one.<P>You can put a roller cam into a non roller block but you will have to do a lot more then just that.  Its not a straight swap.  I wouldn't even recommened doing it unless you get a roller style block<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
Z||000016||DreXteR||10-16-2001||04:20 PM||||Shaun41178 - I understand what you said. Then why the roller lifters are advertised for <B>Chevrolet 60° V-6 80-94, 173 (2.8L)-189 (3.1L)-3.4L</B>?<BR>About the cam and the block, what year/make/model have that type of roller cam block?<P>Thanx<P>DreX||||reg||1
Z||000017||88formula||10-16-2001||06:02 PM||||Talk to Fierosound. He did a 3.4 with a roller cam and used the fiero intake and accessories.  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/calgaryfieros/3400engine.htm</A> <P>||||reg||2
