Z||000024||Shaun41178||10-18-2001||03:53 PM||||Drex yes that link that you posted for the tubo z28 is a mechanical cam and he is using mechanical lifters too.  That is why he can go to 8200 rpm on that engine.  Much harder to do with a hydraulic setup.<P>Yes he will need to readjust the valve lash on that engine.  How often I don't know.  I would email him and find out.  He is the one that told me about the Fiero intake not being able to work with a roller cam.  The camaro lower intake also doesnt' have the oil splash shield on it like the fiero one does and this splash shield will also hit the lifters.<P>Drex I have a good lead on a roller block for really cheap.  Comes with a roller cam too.  Engine block is a 3100 block and was supposed to go into a 95 Grand prix.  I can get it to you for $300 plus shipping.  Oh yea the block and cam is brand new never run.  $300 for a brand new 3100 block and a roller cam is a steal if you ask me.  Shipping will be around $50 or so.  Email me if you have any questions about it or want some more details.  Its in my sig<P><P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR>Shaun41178@hotmail.com<BR>PORN FOREVER!||||reg||1
